<title>DENMARK: Danish Sept North Sea gas production up 25.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish Sept North Sea gas production up 25.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) production of gas from the North Sea rose 25.6 percent to 436 million cubic metres in September from 347 million in August, a spokesman for operator A.P. Moeller Group told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>					   Sept 96     Aug 96   Sept 95</p>
<p>    Output (million cubic metres)  436	   347	 272</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields which make the country the third-biggest producer in western Europe after Norway and Britain.</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc, own 46 percent and 15 percent respectively. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom +45 33 969656</p>
